Subject: [PATCH] cli: a candidate query refused Error_Not_Ready is submitted again within its budget

The controller refuses a candidate query at once with Error_Not_Ready while a radio of the
agent is busy with another command (0207): a topology round, a capability query. On the K8's
soak (rdk-1009, 10 October 02:32Z) one came during a topology round after client churn and
failed the soak with HTTP 503 in 26 ms. That refusal is transient: submitCandidate
(candidate_coordination.go) submits again after 250 ms, then 500 ms, while the request's 8 s
allow, each counted in the coordination timings (not_ready_retries); any other refusal, or the
third, is returned as before.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [lab candidate coordination]

diff --git a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
index f0c41a9..aa656e3 100644
--- a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
@@ -4680,10 +4680,11 @@ func unassocStaQueryHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
     }
 
     var submittedAt uint64
-    timing.nativeStep(func() {
+    // Error_Not_Ready (a radio of the agent busy) submitted again within the request's budget
+    err = submitCandidate(timing, func() error {
         submittedAt = uint64(time.Now().UnixMilli())
-        err = submitCandidateQuery(jsonBytes)
-    })
+        return submitCandidateQuery(jsonBytes)
+    }, started.Add(8*time.Second), time.Sleep)
     if err != nil {
         timing.ElapsedMilliseconds = float64(time.Since(started).Nanoseconds()) / 1e6
         w.Header().Set("Content-Type", "application/json")
